-- title:
--   One winding datum for all K-side Hecke words
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L/K$ finite Galois, $\sigma\colon L\simeq_K L$ is an automorphism such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$ (`hgen`), and $[L:K]$ is prime (`hdeg`); the groups $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over adele rings and the idele groups carry their Borel structures, and `adelicGLHaar` is the Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring in question.
--
--   *Global data over $L$.* Reals $0<\alpha<\beta$ (`hα`, `hαβ`); a set $\Phi_L\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$ lying in the slab where the Tate idele norm of the determinant belongs to $[\alpha,\beta]$ (`hΦs`), which is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ under `globalPoints` acting on that slab with the restricted Haar measure (`hΦ`); a Haar measure $\nu_{Z_L}$ on $\mathbb A_L^\times$ together with a fundamental domain $\Omega_L$ for the image of $L^\times$ (`hΩL`); a datum $D$ of type `IdeleGaloisDescent`, i.e. a homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)\to\mathrm{Aut}(\mathbb A_L)$ which is continuous in each argument and compatible with the embedding of $L$. Finite sets of finite places $S_K$ of $K$ and $S_L$ of $L$ such that every place of $L$ above a place of $S_K$ lies in $S_L$ (`hSL`), membership in $S_L$ depends only on the place of $K$ below (`hSsat`), and every place of $L$ whose place below is outside $S_K$ has ramification index $1$ (`hS`). A character $\xi_L$ of the full idele group of $L$ with values in $\mathbb C^\times$, continuous (`hξc`), trivial on the principal ideles (`hξt`), and taking the same value on $\det\,$`heckeGen`$(w)$ and $\det\,$`heckeGen`$(w')$ whenever $w,w'\notin S_L$ lie above the same place of $K$ (`hξσ`). An ideal $N$ of $\mathcal O_L$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S_L$ (`hN`); an archimedean type family `tysL` for $L$; test-function data $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$ and $\varphi_S$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ for each finite place $v$ of $K$. A compact set $X$ of functions from the finite places of $L$ to $\mathbb C\times\mathbb C$ (`hXc`) containing (`hX`) all $x$ which vanish on $S_L$ and satisfy, for $w\notin S_L$: $(x\,w)_2=\#(\mathcal O_L/w)\cdot\xi_L(\det\,$`heckeGen`$(w))$, $\|(x\,w)_1\|\le(\#(\mathcal O_L/w)+1)\sqrt{\|\xi_L(\det\,\mathrm{heckeGen}(w))\|}$, and $\overline{(x\,w)_1}=\bigl(\overline{(x\,w)_2}/\|(x\,w)_2\|\bigr)(x\,w)_1$.
--
--   *Global data over $K$.* A set $\Phi_K$ in the corresponding norm slab (`hΦKs`) which is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ (`hΦK`); a Haar measure $\nu_{Z_K}$ on $\mathbb A_K^\times$ with fundamental domain $\Omega_K$ for the principal ideles (`hΩK`); a finite set $\Xi$ of characters of the full idele group of $K$, characterised (`hΞ`) as consisting exactly of those $\xi$ which are continuous, trivial on principal ideles, and satisfy $\xi\bigl(\mathrm{idelicNorm}(z)\bigr)=\xi_L(z)$ for all $z\in\mathbb A_L^\times$, the norm being that of `genuineBaseChange K L`. An ideal $N'$ of $\mathcal O_K$ with all prime divisors in $S_K$ (`hN'`); an archimedean type family `tysK`; a constant $c_0\in\mathbb C$.
--
--   *The geometric comparison hypothesis `hgeo`.* For every finite set $S'\supseteq S_K$ of finite places of $K$, every continuous compactly supported $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$ which is unit-factorizable above $S'$ for the level `levelOne (𝓞 L) L N` $\sqcap$ `finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L` and archimedeanly bi-finite of type `tysL`, every continuous compactly supported $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_K)$ which is unit-factorizable at $S'$ for `principalLevel (𝓞 K) K N'` $\sqcap$ `finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup K` and archimedeanly bi-finite of type `tysK`, such that $\varphi$ and $f$ match at $S'$ relative to $\sigma^{-1}$ (existence of semi-local and unit factorizations with matching archimedean and matching local factors at each $v\in S'$), and such that at each $v\notin S'$ all of whose extensions to $L$ are unramified the indicator of the semi-local integral set matches the indicator of the local integral set, one has
--   $$\int_{\Phi_L}\int_{\Omega_L}\xi_L(z)\!\!\sum_{\delta}\varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\,\delta\,\sigma^{-1}\!\cdot(c(z)x)\bigr)\,d\nu_{Z_L}\,d\mu_L = c_0\sum_{\xi_K\in\Xi}\int_{\Phi_K}\int_{\Omega_K}\xi_K(z)\bigl(K^{\mathrm{cen}}_f(x,c(z)x)+K^{\mathrm{ell}}_f(x,c(z)x)\bigr)d\nu_{Z_K}\,d\mu_K,$$
--   where the finite sum runs over those $\delta\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted conjugacy class is carried by the twisted norm class map `normClassMap hgen` to the conjugacy class of some $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ which is either scalar or has characteristic polynomial without roots in $K$, $c(\cdot)$ denotes the central scalar embedding, and $K^{\mathrm{cen}}_f$, $K^{\mathrm{ell}}_f$ are the central and elliptic parts of the adelic kernel, i.e. the finite sums of $f(x^{-1}\gamma y)$ over scalar $\gamma$, respectively over $\gamma$ with no eigenvalue in $K$.
--
--   *Hecke places and local coset data.* A finite set $T$ of finite places of $K$ disjoint from $S_K$ (`hTdisj`) with $|T|\ge 2$ (`hT2`) such that no place of $L$ above a place of $T$ lies in $S_L$ (`hTSL`); a choice $w_v=$ `ws v` of an extension to $L$ of each place $v$; a map $v\mapsto w'_v$ with $(w'_v)=\sigma^{-1}\!\cdot(w_v)$ as ideals for $v\in T$ (`hw'`). Over $L$: elements $\varpi_v$ of the valuation ring of the $w_v$-adic completion, irreducible with nonzero image for $v\in T$ (`hϖirr`, `hϖs0`); families $r_{T,v}\colon\mathrm{Fin}(n_v)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ forming, for $v\in T$, a complete irredundant system of cosets of the integral subgroup inside the double coset of [`LocalGL2.diagPi`](def/LocalLanglands_HeckeCosetLocal.html#L68) $(\varpi_v)$ (`hrTs`); elements $z_v$ equal to the scalar matrix $\varpi_v\cdot 1$ for $v\in T$ (`hzs`). Over $K$: the exact analogues $\varpi_{K,v}$, $n_{K,v}$, $r_{K,v}$, $z_{K,v}$ with the same hypotheses (`hϖKirr`, `hϖKs0`, `hrKs`, `hzKs`). Further: every $\xi\in\Xi$ is unramified outside $S_K$, in the sense that it kills the idele supported at $v\notin S_K$ with a unit entry of valuation $1$ (`hur`); for $v\in T$ the absolute norms of $w_v$ and $w'_v$ agree (`hNw'`) and equal $\#(\mathcal O_K/v)^{\,d_v}$ with $d_v=$ `slotDeg K L ws v` the inertia degree of $w_v$ over $v$ (`hNwf'`); complex numbers $s_v$ with $s_v^2=\xi_L(\det\,$`heckeGen`$(w'_v))$ for $v\in T$ (`hs`); and for every $\xi\in\Xi$ and $v\in T$, $\xi(\det\,$`heckeGen`$(v))^{d_v}=\xi_L(\det\,$`heckeGen`$(w'_v))$ (`hxK`).
--
--   *Standing analytic data on the $K$ side.* An archimedean test factor $f_{a,K}$, smooth in the archimedean matrix entries and compactly supported (`hfaK`), and local test functions $f_{S,K}(v)$, locally constant with compact support, for $v\in S_K$ (`hfSK`); reals $\kappa_0^K,\kappa^K$ and $c_{\tau K}>0$ (`hcτK`); a measure $\nu_A$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $K$ and a constant $c_G$ for which the product formula `hG` holds: for each finite $S$ and each $f,f_a,f_S$ with the stated measurability, with $f(g)=f_a(g_\infty)\prod_{v\in S}f_S(v)(g_v)$ whenever all components of $g$ outside $S$ are integral and $f(g)=0$ otherwise, the adelic Haar integral of $f$ equals $c_G(\int f_a\,d\nu_A)\prod_{v\in S}\int f_S(v)\,d\mu_v$. Measures $\tau_G(u,z)$ on the centralizer of $c(z)\,\mathrm{diag}(u,1)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_K)$, Haar for $u\neq1$ (`hτG`), with $\int g\,d\tau_G(u,z)=c_{\tau K}\int g(\mathrm{diag}(p_1,p_2))\,d(\nu_{Z_K}\times\nu_{Z_K})$ for $u\neq 1$ (`hτGc`); measures $\tau_A(u,z)$ on the centralizer of the archimedean component, Haar for $u\neq1$ (`hτA`); measures $\tau_F(u,z,v)$ on the local centralizer at $v$ of the $v$-component, Haar for $u\neq1$ (`hτF`) and giving mass $1$ to the preimage of the local integral set (`hτF1`); a constant $c_T>0$ (`hcT`) for which the corresponding product formula `hT` holds on the centralizers: for $u\neq1$, $z$, finite $S$ and functions $W,W_a,W_S$ with the stated measurability, factorization over integral components and vanishing otherwise, $\int W\,d\tau_G(u,z)=c_T(\int W_a\,d\tau_A(u,z))\prod_{v\in S}\int W_S(v)\,d\tau_F(u,z,v)$. Finally, functions $I_A$ and $I_F$ realising, for $u\neq1$, the orbital integral of $f_{a,K}$ at the archimedean component (`hIA`) and, for $v\in S_K$, the orbital integral of $f_{S,K}(v)$ at the $v$-component (`hIF`) of $c(z)\,\mathrm{diag}(u,1)$, in the sense of `IsOrbitalIntegralOn` and `IsOrbitalIntegral` (existence of a section weight $w$ with $I=\int f(x^{-1}\gamma x)w(x)$); and a constant $\kappa_m\in\mathbb C$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* There exists a winding datum $\mathcal A$ of signature $(r,d,c)$ with $r$ the number of infinite places of $K$, $d=|T|$ and $c=r+|T|$ — that is, a discrete subgroup $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb R^{r}\times\mathbb Z^{d}$ with a linear functional and frequency vector satisfying the stated pairing identity, a character of $\Lambda$ into $(\mathbb R/\mathbb Z)^{c}$, a chain of subgroups, and sequences of continuous integrable test functions on $\mathbb R^{r}$ with the prescribed quadratic decay of the functions and of their Fourier transforms, together with the remaining coefficient data — such that the following holds for all exponent functions $k,j$ on the finite places of $K$ and all further data as listed.
--
--   Given a family `fam` of functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_K)$ indexed by the slot multi-indices $m$ in `slotIndex K L ws k j T` (the product over $v\in T$ of the supports of `slotWord K L ws v (k v) (j v)`), subject to `hfam`: for each such $m$ there is a finite test factor $f\!f$ (locally constant, compactly supported) which vanishes at any $h$ having a non-integral component outside $S_K\cup T$, which at $h$ with all components outside $S_K\cup T$ integral equals $\prod_{v\in S_K\cup T}$ of the $v$-component evaluated at $f_{S,K}(v)$ for $v\notin T$ and, for $v\in T$, at the function $x\mapsto\sum_{\iota}\mathbf 1_{\mathrm{integral}}\bigl((\prod r_{K,v}(\iota(\cdot))\,z_{K,v}^{\,m_v(1)})^{-1}x\bigr)$, the sum being over all maps $\iota\colon\mathrm{Fin}(m_v(0))\to\mathrm{Fin}(n_{K,v})$ and the product being the ordered product of the chosen coset representatives; and such that `fam` $m$ factors as $g\mapsto f_{a,K}(g_\infty)\,f\!f(g_{\mathrm{fin}})$. Given further a finite set $\Delta_K\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ of diagonal matrices with eigenvalue ratio $\neq1$ (`hΔK`) on which the ratio map is injective (`hΔKinj`); Haar measures $\tau_K(\gamma)$ on the centralizer of the image of $\gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_K)$ (`hτK`) satisfying, for $\gamma\in\Delta_K$, the same reduction to $\nu_{Z_K}\times\nu_{Z_K}$ with constant $c_{\tau K}$ (`hτKc`); functions $I_K(m,\gamma,z)$ realising the orbital integral of $g\mapsto$ `fam` $m\,(c(z)g)$ at the global point $\gamma$ with respect to the adelic Haar measure and $\tau_K(\gamma)$, for $m$ a slot index and $\gamma\in\Delta_K$ (`hIK`); and the exhaustion hypothesis `hΔKc`: for each slot index $m$ and each $u\in K^\times$, $u\neq1$, whose value is not the eigenvalue ratio of any $\gamma\in\Delta_K$, one has `fam` $m\bigl(x^{-1}c(z)\mathrm{diag}(u,1)x\bigr)=0$ for all $z$ and $x$. Then
--   $$\kappa_m\sum_{\xi\in\Xi}\ \sum_{m}\ \mathrm{slotFamilyCoeff}(m)\sum_{\gamma\in\Delta_K}\kappa_0^K\Bigl(\kappa^K\int_{\mathbb A_K^\times}\xi(z)\,I_K(m,\gamma,z)\,d\nu_{Z_K}\Bigr) =\sum_{n}\Bigl(\prod_{i}\bigl(\sqrt{\#(\mathcal O_L/w'_{v_i})}\;s_{v_i}\bigr)^{k_{v_i}}\,\xi_L\bigl(\det\,\mathrm{heckeGen}(w'_{v_i})\bigr)^{j_{v_i}}\,\bigl[(T+T^{-1})^{k_{v_i}}\bigr]_{n_i}\Bigr)\,\mathcal A.\mathrm{coeff}(n),$$
--   where $m$ runs over `slotIndex K L ws k j T`, the slot coefficient is $\mathrm{slotFamilyCoeff}(m)=\prod_{v\in T}$ `slotCoeff K L ws v (k v) (j v) (m v)`, the index $n$ runs over the box $\prod_{i}[-k_{v_i},k_{v_i}]\cap\mathbb Z$ indexed by $i\in\mathrm{Fin}|T|$ via the canonical enumeration $v_i$ of $T$, $[\cdot]_{n_i}$ denotes the coefficient of the Laurent polynomial $(T+T^{-1})^{k_{v_i}}$ over $\mathbb C$ in degree $n_i$, and $\mathcal A.\mathrm{coeff}(n)=\sum_{i\in\mathbb N}\mathcal A.\mathrm{lam}(i)\cdot\mathcal A.\mathrm{fibreCoeff}(i,n)$. The winding datum $\mathcal A$ is chosen before $k$, $j$, `fam`, $\Delta_K$, $\tau_K$ and $I_K$, so a single datum serves every Hecke word.
--
--   This is the $K$-side packaging step in the comparison of split (hyperbolic) terms in the base-change trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension of prime degree: the weighted sums of $\xi$-twisted orbital integrals over the diagonal classes attached to an arbitrary Hecke word are expressed, uniformly in that word, as a finite Satake-Laurent combination of the coefficients of one winding datum. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_const_forall_exists_windingDatum_sub_finrank_mul_const_mul_sum_eq_sum_mul_coeff_of_hyperbolicTerm_eq_affine`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_const_forall_exists_windingDatum_sub_finrank_mul_const_mul_sum_eq_sum_mul_coeff_of_hyperbolicTerm_eq_affine) in the route to cyclic base change for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ underlying the Langlands–Tunnell theorem.
